      "lustretype": "Metallic",
      "aboutname": "Named in antiquity from the Greek \"pyr\" for \"fire\", because sparks flew from it when struck with another mineral or metal. Known to Dioscorides (~50 CE) and mentioned in book 5 of his 5-volume work \"περι υληζ ιατρικηζ\" (transliteration: \"Peri hulēs iatrikēs\"), both meaning \"On Medical Material\". \"Purites lithos\" (an umbrella term for both pyrite and chalcopyrite) was used (together with honey) to treat skin problems.",
